<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pike</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as pikemen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The pike is a long thrusting spear used by infantry in close formations, especially to resist cavalry. In early modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> it was combined with firearms in mixed formations. Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tercio">tercios</a> of pikemen and arquebusiers gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> military dominance for over a century, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> reorganised pike and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musket</a> into smaller, more mobile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">brigades</a>.</p></div>
